\section{Identification}{


In \code{y = X \%*\% beta + f(Z) + e} a constant can move freely between \code{f} and an
intercept, so the two are not separately identified. \code{center_f = TRUE} pins
this down by centring the realised \code{f(Z)} to sample mean zero. \code{X} carries no
intercept column for the same reason.
